From 4a39dbfe57a6a50f08860c5f37b85a5f8e97d333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:01:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] Keep Blu-ray menu overlays separate from
 subtitles

Blu-ray menus drawn by libbluray share the overlay container with
subtitles, and subtitle handling removes or hides them: opening or
closing a subtitle stream clears the whole container, a new subtitle
sets the end time of the menu, and a forced subtitle replaces it.
libbluray only redraws a menu when it changes, so the menu stays hidden
until the user navigates.

Mark the overlays the Blu-ray input stream draws as disc menu overlays.
Subtitle stream changes now clear only subtitle overlays, subtitles and
disc menus no longer end or replace each other, and disc menus are
drawn above subtitles and do not count towards the subtitle queue
limit. The container is still fully cleared when the player exits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

[Hades: adapted to Piers, where the Blu-ray input stream hands its menu overlays to the player with m_player->OnDiscNavResult() rather than NotifyPlayer(); the includes and the test of TestVideoPlayer.cpp placed by hand, its context there differs. Same lines added and removed as the origin, d620f5654180.]
